13
00:00:43,720 --> 00:00:46,920
Okay, for starters we have Tom Yum soup.

14
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:48,830
It's a bit spicy but really good.

15
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:50,150
This is delicious.

16
00:00:50,810 --> 00:00:53,310
The ginger and lemongrass really give it a nice taste.

17
00:00:53,810 --> 00:00:56,810
Now this next dish is one of the most famous.

18
00:00:57,410 --> 00:01:01,410
Foreigners call it papaya salad but the proper name is Tom Sam.

19
00:01:02,230 --> 00:01:09,810
It is a spicy salad made from a mix of fresh vegetables including shredded unripened papaya and tomato.

20
00:01:10,350 --> 00:01:11,230
This is delicious.

21
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:15,220
The combination of sour and spicy is really interesting.

22
00:01:15,250 --> 00:01:16,390
I could have this every day.

23
00:01:16,870 --> 00:01:21,050
Okay, now for the last and best dish in my opinion.

24
00:01:21,570 --> 00:01:23,090
This is called Pad Thai.

25
00:01:23,930 --> 00:01:36,270
Stir fried noodles with eggs, fish sauce, tamarind juice, red chili pepper plus bean sprouts, shrimp and tofu garnished with crushed peanuts and coriander.

26
00:01:36,890 --> 00:01:38,850
It's practically Thailand's national dish.

27
00:01:39,430 --> 00:01:40,530
Wow, this is great.

28
00:01:40,870 --> 00:01:43,190
I never knew Thai food was so creative and delicious.

29
