33
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:01,070
Language takeaway.

34
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:07,720
All right, so the first word we have on language takeaway today is food poisoning.

35
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:11,240
So we don't want to get food poisoning when having this, any meal.

36
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:12,060
Any meal, no, that's right.

37
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:14,280
Food poisoning is a bad thing.

38
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:18,460
Now this is something that happens when you eat bad food or dirty food.

39
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:24,240
So you get very, very sick and you feel like you have to vomit, you have to throw up.

40
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:25,240
That's right.

41
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:29,960
So your stomach hurts, you feel like you have to throw up, you may be going to the bathroom very often.

42
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:31,840
That means usually you have food poisoning.

43
00:02:32,720 --> 00:02:38,360
All right, and so people often associate food poisoning with food that you eat on the street, maybe dirtier food.

44
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:44,340
But this is something you should be very careful of when you're traveling, not to Thailand alone, but maybe to any other country.

45
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:46,700
You can get it in America, you can get it in Mexico.

46
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:48,180
So just something to be careful of.

47
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:48,860
That's right.

48
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:54,460
So apart from that, we're going to jump into our first dish for today.

49
00:02:54,640 --> 00:02:56,720
