50
00:02:57,320 --> 00:02:58,320
Tom Yum Soup.

51
00:02:58,320 --> 00:02:59,820
Now this is one of my favorite soups.

52
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:01,700
It's quite spicy, isn't it, Marco?

53
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:05,300
Very spicy, but very, very good as well.

54
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:09,640
It has a kind of citric taste, like a lemon.

55
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:12,100
It does, and it's very yellow or orange colored.

56
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:16,340
And it's a very, very common dish on Thai restaurant menus.

57
00:03:17,380 --> 00:03:21,640
And there are some key ingredients in this soup that I think are important to discuss.

58
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:24,320
They're often found in Thai food and other kinds of Asian food.

59
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:25,610
The first one is ginger.

60
00:03:26,030 --> 00:03:26,910
Ginger, that's right.

61
00:03:27,110 --> 00:03:27,790
This is a root.

62
00:03:28,230 --> 00:03:30,350
It kind of looks like a potato almost.

63
00:03:30,750 --> 00:03:31,130
It does.

64
00:03:31,980 --> 00:03:35,080
It's usually white and it has little arms, you know.

65
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:36,130
It's not a round object.

66
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:38,080
It's got pointy little arms.

67
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:38,230
That's right.

68
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:44,240
And the characteristic taste of ginger is kind of strong and bitter.

69
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:44,830
It is quite strong.

70
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:46,720
You'll find it in Japanese food.

71
00:03:46,720 --> 00:03:48,720
Sometimes you get pickled ginger to eat.

72
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:51,440
It's like a pink food you get with sushi.

73
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:56,380
Other times in Chinese cooking, it's something that's chopped up with garlic and cooked in oil.

74
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:59,000
So ginger is a very important one.

75
00:03:59,000 --> 00:03:59,160
That's right.

76
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,760
So in this soup, we have ginger and we also have lemongrass.

77
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:06,620
So this is very interesting because it's not very easily found around the world.

78
00:04:06,900 --> 00:04:07,360
That's right.

79
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:09,980
This is very common in Southeast Asian cooking.

80
00:04:09,980 --> 00:04:15,340
And you might have a hard time finding it in places like America where it's not really a part of the cuisine.

81
00:04:15,820 --> 00:04:17,620
But lemongrass is very distinct.

82
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:21,380
It has a very strong flavor and it's actually quite long.

83
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:22,700
It's green and long.

84
00:04:22,940 --> 00:04:24,800
It looks a bit like celery, but it's harder.

85
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:25,760
That's right.

86
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:27,520
That's right.

87
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:32,160
And the taste that it gives it is a little bit citric, kind of like a lemon almost.

88
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:32,320
That's right.

89
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:35,460
But you're going to find this in soups like tom yum or other things.

90
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:38,720
So lemongrass is another one.

91
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:46,860
And then moving on to our next dish, which is one of the most, I think, the most popular dishes of all Thailand is the famous pad thai.

92
00:04:47,880 --> 00:04:48,150
Pad thai.

93
00:04:48,880 --> 00:04:51,030
Now, this is absolutely my favorite Thai dish.

94
00:04:51,030 --> 00:04:52,510
And I know that's very cliche.

95
00:04:52,990 --> 00:04:55,170
It's something that everyone says, but it's true.

96
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:57,560
You know, this is a great dish you can buy on the street.

97
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:58,470
You can buy it in a restaurant.

98
00:04:59,180 --> 00:05:00,510
It's basically a noodle dish, right?

99
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:01,290
That's right.

100
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:06,770
It's stir fried noodles with eggs and peanuts are the most, like the key ingredients in there.

101
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:08,600
That's right.

102
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:12,140
But you might also get a little bit of hot red pepper, some sugar, some lime.

103
00:05:12,140 --> 00:05:13,190
And the noodles are flat.

104
00:05:13,640 --> 00:05:14,130
They're not round.

105
00:05:14,470 --> 00:05:14,970
That's right.

106
00:05:15,430 --> 00:05:20,770
