107
00:05:21,350 --> 00:05:21,590
All right.

108
00:05:21,830 --> 00:05:22,430
Tamarind juice.

109
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:28,670
This is again another one of those flavors from Southeast Asia that you might not find in many other places, certainly not in America.

110
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:31,490
Now tamarind, they're funny looking things.

111
00:05:31,490 --> 00:05:33,650
They look like peas, but they're dark brown.

112
00:05:34,250 --> 00:05:34,850
That's right.

113
00:05:35,110 --> 00:05:38,410
So tamarind juice gives it this kind of sweet flavor.

114
00:05:38,830 --> 00:05:46,570
So this is the interesting thing about pad thai is that you have these sweet flavors from the tamarind juice, from even the fish sauce combined with chili.

115
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:49,520
So it's kind of like a spicy, very sweet taste.

116
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:51,080
And then you have citrus.

117
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:52,640
You have some lime maybe and some sugar.

118
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:58,360
So it's a lot of different tastes and flavors, but it's a really magical combination.

119
00:05:58,360 --> 00:05:58,480
That's right.

120
00:05:59,360 --> 00:06:00,540
