153
00:07:34,280 --> 00:07:34,560
Fluency Builder.

154
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:38,130
So first up we have the phrase on the menu.

155
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:39,850
What's on the menu tonight?

156
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:41,880
That's right.

157
00:07:41,880 --> 00:07:43,730
That person asked, so what's on the menu?

158
00:07:44,080 --> 00:07:47,240
And by saying this, we're saying, well, what are we having for dinner?

159
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:48,660
What are we going to eat?

160
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:49,160
That's right.

161
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:54,920
So you might want to think, okay, menu, I'm going to look at the menu, but you could even say this at home where there is no menu.

162
00:07:55,520 --> 00:07:58,840
This is a spoken language way of saying, what are we eating tonight?

163
00:07:59,200 --> 00:07:59,400
Right.

164
00:07:59,620 --> 00:07:59,880
That's right.

165
00:08:00,020 --> 00:08:00,480
What's for dinner?

166
00:08:01,420 --> 00:08:02,120
What are we eating?

167
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:03,400
What's on the menu?

168
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:05,100
